<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Athan Dial on Athan Dial — AI product leadership for expert work</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/</link><description>Recent content in Athan Dial on Athan Dial — AI product leadership for expert work</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://athan-dial.github.io/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>An all-false column is a legal column</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/notes/an-all-false-column-is-a-legal-column/</link><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/notes/an-all-false-column-is-a-legal-column/</guid><description>A one-character naming mismatch made a boolean false for every row. Five layers each behaved correctly and nothing threw. The only check that caught it was a person who knew the answer was impossible.</description></item><item><title>The Outer Loop</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/essays/the-outer-loop/</link><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/essays/the-outer-loop/</guid><description>AI makes the plan-build-verify loop faster, which also makes it easier to perfect the wrong product. The outer loop keeps the user, the problem, and the product shape open to question — and it matters more now that the expert can arrive with a prototype.</description></item><item><title>The primary user was not in the room</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/work/intelligence-platform-for-an-absent-user/</link><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/work/intelligence-platform-for-an-absent-user/</guid><description>I designed and helped build an internal intelligence platform that reconciled records from multiple sources without asking a model to decide what was true. A discovery conversation changed the primary user from the analyst to a leadership function. That reframe clarified the product boundary: the machine could retrieve, rank, and propose; the analyst still had to adjudicate. The platform eventually reached production after an earlier attempt failed at a permissions boundary.</description></item><item><title>When a Faster Search Tool Still Felt Incomplete</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/work/analog-search-as-a-product/</link><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/work/analog-search-as-a-product/</guid><description>I led the product definition for an analog-search tool that made warmed-database queries roughly an order of magnitude faster after an implementation change. Then its primary expert user said a commercial alternative returned more results. My proposed response was not to claim parity. It was to give the expert threshold control and make the edge of a match visible.</description></item><item><title>When Measurement Cannot Choose for You</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/essays/the-operating-layer/</link><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/essays/the-operating-layer/</guid><description>Some model choices cannot be settled by a fair comparison. The honest response is to write down the strategic argument, the uncertainty, and what would change your mind.</description></item><item><title>About</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/about/</link><pubDate>Tue, 20 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/about/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The path from bench science to product wasn&amp;rsquo;t planned. The transferable skill turned out to be &lt;strong&gt;designing decision systems under uncertainty&lt;/strong&gt;: figuring out what counts as evidence, which experiment is worth the cost, and how to keep a team&amp;rsquo;s confidence calibrated when truth comes back late or partial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="experience"&gt;Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I describe the job as a fusion of product and data: making sure the company builds the right
things, on time, with good evidence behind each decision.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Redirect to /about/#conversations</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/advisory/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/advisory/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Redirect to /about/#conversations</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/consulting/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/consulting/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Redirect to /thinking/</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/agency/dispatches/ai-research-that-actually-cites-sources/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/agency/dispatches/ai-research-that-actually-cites-sources/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Redirect to /thinking/</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/agency/dispatches/autonomous-agents-need-a-foreman/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/agency/dispatches/autonomous-agents-need-a-foreman/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Redirect to /thinking/</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/agency/dispatches/cowork-changed-how-i-think-about-ai/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/agency/dispatches/cowork-changed-how-i-think-about-ai/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Redirect to /thinking/</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/agency/dispatches/delegation-is-the-real-skill/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/agency/dispatches/delegation-is-the-real-skill/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Redirect to /thinking/</title><link>https://athan-dial.github.io/agency/dispatches/memory-across-sessions/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://athan-dial.github.io/agency/dispatches/memory-across